// v1.1.0.7 Windows - Add real provider question modes, bound consent and offline formula reading.
// v1.1.0.3 Windows - Reuse the desktop entry and save drafts before handing off to a newer release.
// v1.1.0.2 Windows - Load verified workspaces asynchronously and isolate content caches and legal tasks.
// v1.0.3.17 Windows - Queue timer actions without blocking input and reuse navigation cache.
// v1.0.3.16 Windows - Reduce repeated live projection and reminder work during input frames.
// v1.0.3.12 Windows - Avoid whole-body copies when building note list metadata and previews.
// v1.0.3.10 Windows - Flush pending database properties before leaving an editor.
// v1.0.3.8 Windows - Borrow unchanged sticky blocks and copy text only on edit.
// v1.0.3.3 Windows - Add a knowledge canvas collection and its persisted workspace state.
// v1.0.2.1 - Reuse verified startup data and reduce autosave and navigation frame work.
// v1.0.2.0 - Make appearance cards report actual selection changes.
// v1.0.1.9 - Repaint the desktop immediately after an appearance selection.
// v1.0.1.8 - Keep theme receipts lightweight on the GUI thread.
// v1.0.1.7 - Persist appearance changes outside the GUI thread.
// v1.0.1.6 - Increment the independent Windows release sequence.
// v1.0.1.5 - Avoid redundant appearance saves on repeated card clicks.
// v1.0.1.4 - Preserve standalone IME punctuation at sentence ends.
// v1.0.1.3 - Improve selected-text contrast in knowledge editors.
// v1.0.1.2 - Restore punctuation input in knowledge editors.
// v1.0.1.1 - Surface manual sync failures and restore legacy workspace startup.
// v2.22.56 - Authenticate local sync peers and finish note privacy cleanup before reporting success.
// v2.22.54 - Reuse read models and avoid copying entire notes during rendering and batched edits.
// v2.22.52 - Preserve structured knowledge pages through editing and persistence.
// v2.22.51 - Keep locally due reminders when synchronized history changes.
// v2.22.50 - Preserve unchanged editor sessions and rebase synced reminder totals.
// v2.22.48 - Align primary navigation with Android and keep timer history inside its parent module.
// v2.22.47 - Align Windows functionality with the Android prototype.
// v2.22.44 - Schedule automatic timer phase commits on the persistence worker.
// v2.22.41 - Preserve knowledge input, edit history and collection navigation.
#![cfg_attr(
    all(windows, not(debug_assertions), not(test)),
    windows_subsystem = "windows"
)]
